.TH CNTX 1 "2026-09-17" "cntx 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cntx \- BYOK, token-efficient AI coding assistant for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cntx
.RI [options]
.RI [PROMPT...]
.br
.B cntx
.I subcommand
.RI [args]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cntx
is a terminal AI coding assistant. You configure an AI provider (bring your
own key); cntx reads, writes, and edits files and runs shell commands inside
your project sandbox under permission modes you control.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode
Approval mode: auto-approve (default), all-approve, manual-approve,
file-only, counsel.
.TP
.B \-\-model
Model id or alias for this prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-endpoint
Endpoint name to use.
.TP
.B \-\-effort
Investigation depth: low, medium, high.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Block file writes and shell execution; preview only.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-write
PATH: add a writable directory outside the project root (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-refresh\-models
Refresh model lists from configured provider APIs.
.TP
.B \-\-chat\-only
Run text-only: no file writes or shell commands.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B init
First-run provider/endpoint/key/model setup.
.TP
.B endpoint
Create, list, change, remove endpoints; \-\-set\-primary, \-\-import.
.TP
.B api-key
Add, list (masked), change, delete provider keys in the local secrets file.
.TP
.B provider
Custom provider presets; install\-preset.
.TP
.B model, config, session, memory, mcp, skill
Model aliases and cache, configuration, sessions, project memory, MCP
servers, reusable skills.
.TP
.B bench
Estimate optimization, routing, and rough cost without calling a model.
.TP
.B doctor
Config, keys, and environment diagnostics (\-\-fix repairs; \-\-verify runs
the full test suite).
.TP
.B completions
Generate shell completions.
.TP
.B man
Print this manual page. Install it with:
.B cntx man > \e$(dirname \e$(manpath 2>/dev/null | head -1) 2>/dev/null || echo /usr/local/share/man/man1)/cntx.1
or simply: cntx man | sudo tee /usr/local/share/man/man1/cntx.1
.SH APPROVAL MODES
auto-approve (default): reads and in-project writes run without prompts;
shell commands ask with
.B y
(allow once),
.B ya
(allow commands for the rest of the session),
.B n
(decline).
all-approve: everything permitted runs without prompting.
manual-approve: every tool asks first.
file-only: files allowed (in-sandbox), shell/network denied.
counsel: token-efficient model mix; same approval behavior as auto-approve.
File edits are always confined to the project root unless widened with
.B \-\-allow\-write
or disabled with
.B \-\-dangerously\-disable\-sandbox
(not recommended). The sandbox is application policy, not OS isolation.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, OLLAMA_API_KEY
Provider API keys; or store keys with cntx api-key add.
.TP
.B CNTX_CONFIG_DIR
Override the configuration directory (default:
$HOME/Library/Application Support/cntxcode on macOS, $HOME/.config/cntxcode
on Linux).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $CNTX_CONFIG_DIR/secrets.yaml
API keys (mode 0600).
.TP
.I $CNTX_CONFIG_DIR/config.yaml
Endpoints, primary selection, routing settings.
.TP
.I .cntx/memory.md, AGENTS.md
Project memory and instructions loaded per session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
cntx init \-\-provider anthropic
Configure Anthropic.
.TP
cntx "add pagination to the users endpoint and run the tests"
One-shot task with tools.
.TP
cntx \-\-mode manual\-approve "show me what you would change"
Ask before every step.
